  "note": "Triennial election of the Portstewart Urban District Council, polled 17 May 1967. Fourteen candidates were nominated for the twelve seats; four retiring members (S. A. Moss, J. Vance, N. M. Gibson and G. C. Parlato) did not seek re-election. The newcomer Donald Alexander Bell topped the poll with 997 votes. Completed in the meetings gap-fill, 7 Nov 2026. Names are the full forms of the nomination list; the result prints initials ('R. Taylor' is R. F. Taylor). Neill is printed 'H. R. Neil' in the nomination list. No labels printed."
